/* Modern theme for the server-select dialog -- flat programmatic chrome, no legacy sprite art.
   Same DOM/class structure as the legacy theme (server_select.rml is shared); only the visual
   treatment differs, same convention as char_make.rcss's modern copy. #panel itself stays
   invisible here too -- see the legacy theme's own comment for why (matches the real legacy
   screen, not a modern redesign choice). #panel also deliberately has no explicit height here --
   see the legacy theme's own comment for why (it must auto-size to #group_row's real footprint,
   not mirror ServerSelWin.h's oversized native-click-gate rect, or .center-both centers the wrong
   box). */

/* No explicit position here -- .center-both (base.rcss) supplies position:absolute plus the
   left/top/transform centering math, same as sys_menu.rcss/msg_win.rcss's own #panel -- see the
   legacy theme's own copy of this comment for why this matches that precedent exactly. */
#panel {
	width: 500px;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
	font-size: 12px;
	color: token(text-body);
	padding: 10px;
}

#group_row {
	position: relative;
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: row;
	justify-content: space-between;
	width: 480px;
	height: 400px;
	padding-top: 34px;
}
/* #group_row's own height is a fixed worst-case reservation (10 groups per column --
   ServerSelWin.cpp caps leftGroups/rightGroups at 10 each), not the real button count, so the
   real buttons must be vertically centered within it (not packed to its top) -- otherwise a
   typical, mostly-empty column looks pinned near the top of #panel once .center-both centers
   that oversized row, most visibly at smaller window heights. */
#left_col, #right_col {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	justify-content: center;
}
#test_server_btn {
	position: absolute;
	left: 50%;
	top: 50%;
	transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}

/* Crimson base instead of .server-row's warm charcoal -- the dark charcoal read too close to the
   dark backdrop/video behind this screen to stand out. Reuses base.rcss's own .btn-ok
   accent-crimson palette verbatim (same gradient stops and border-color/border-top-color bevel
   values) rather than inventing a new one-off color. Childless, so there's no border-width+children
   risk here (unlike .server-row below). .checked has no equivalent state on .server-row (which has
   no persistent-selection concept) -- it gets a full gold border instead of just the top bevel
   edge, so the currently-selected group reads as clearly different from a merely-hovered one.

   height is 30px, not literally 32px -- `height` sets content size only, and this rule's own
   1px+1px border is added on top of it: 30 + 1 + 1 = 32, matching .server-row's own real height
   below. ServerSelWin.cpp's kGroupBtnRowHeight (36px = that real height + margin-bottom) must stay
   in sync with it (and with the legacy theme's own copy of this rule, since both themes share that
   one C++ constant), or the server-list flyout docks at the wrong row for whichever theme doesn't
   match it. */
.group-btn {
	position: relative;
	width: 108px;
	height: 30px;
	margin-bottom: 4px;
	text-align: center;
	vertical-align: middle;
	line-height: 30px;
	cursor: pointer;
	pointer-events: auto;
	background-color: #430e17;
	decorator: linear-gradient(to bottom, token(accent-crimson-bright), token(accent-crimson) 35%, #6c1520 70%, #430e17); /* bright/base stops are real tokens; the two darker stops are derived shades with no token of their own */
	border-width: 1px;
	border-color: #0a0706;
	border-top-color: rgba(211, 74, 94, 115); /* accent-crimson-bright's rgb @ 115 alpha */
	border-radius: token(radius-sm)px;
	color: token(text-emphasis);
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
}
.group-btn:hover {
	decorator: linear-gradient(to bottom, #e05f72, token(accent-crimson-bright) 35%, #8c1e2c 70%, #571219); /* #e05f72 is a brighter-than-token hover-only highlight, no token */
	border-color: #e05f72;
}
.group-btn.checked {
	decorator: linear-gradient(to bottom, #e05f72, token(accent-crimson-bright) 35%, #8c1e2c 70%, #571219);
	border-color: token(accent-gold-bright);
	color: token(text-title);
}

/* Flyout: absent until a group is clicked, then docks beside that specific button -- see
   ServerSelRmlModel's own comment (ServerSelWin.h). top is always pushed from C++
   (data-style-top); dock-left/dock-right/dock-center below only resolve the horizontal side, since
   an inline data-style-top always wins over any class rule's own top. No background/border/padding
   of its own -- the .server-row buttons stacked inside it are enough on their own, no enclosing
   panel needed; width matches .server-row's own border-box size (218px width + 20px padding + 2px
   border = 240px) directly since there's no padding gutter to size around anymore. */
#server_list {
	position: absolute;
	width: 240px;
	max-height: 352px;
	overflow: hidden auto;
}
#server_list.dock-left {
	left: 118px;
}
#server_list.dock-right {
	right: 118px;
}
#server_list.dock-center {
	left: 50%;
	transform: translateX(-50%);
}

/* The gauge bar reads as *inside* the same button frame as the name, not a separate bar underneath
   -- so .server-row carries the border/gradient itself, containing both its own text content and
   its one child, .server-gauge-slot. Unlike the legacy theme's equivalent (a decorator-only
   ninepatch, no border-width property at all), this uses a real CSS `border-width` on an element
   that has a child -- a combination not confirmed safe in this RmlUi build (see STATUS.md's
   bordered-element-plus-children finding). If the frame ever renders as an incomplete/non-closed
   rectangle, the border needs to move to a decorator-based construction (e.g. a second, inset
   decorator layer) instead of border-width/border-*-color.

   Raised-metal look: .modern-frame's own bevel mechanism (base.rcss's header comment) --
   decorator:linear-gradient fill plus per-side border-color bevel (light top/left, dark
   bottom/right), standing in for a box-shadow inset highlight that this engine's render interface
   doesn't composite (see STATUS.md). Same warm charcoal gradient as the legacy theme's own
   .server-row -- a one-off palette, not token-driven.

   height is 23px, not .group-btn's real 32px -- `height` sets content size only; padding and
   border-width both add on top of it. 23 + this row's 3px+4px padding + 1px+1px border = 32,
   matching .group-btn's real on-screen height.

   width is a literal px value (218 = this row's border-box target of 240px, matching #server_list's
   own width, minus this row's own 10px+10px padding and 1px+1px border). .server-gauge-slot has
   neither padding nor border, so its width is the direct target (200px), inset by a literal 10px
   left margin to center it within .server-row's own 218px content width. margin-bottom is 1px, not
   .group-btn's 4px, for tighter stacking since #server_list no longer has an enclosing panel. */
.server-row {
	display: block;
	position: relative;
	width: 218px;
	height: 23px;
	margin-bottom: 1px;
	padding: 3px 10px 4px;
	text-align: center;
	line-height: 14px;
	white-space: nowrap;
	cursor: pointer;
	pointer-events: auto;
	background-color: #0a0d10;
	decorator: linear-gradient(to bottom, #1a2027, #0a0d10 48%, #12151a); /* cool neutral, was warm charcoal -- structural framing goes cool now */
	border-width: 1px;
	border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 50);
	border-left-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 50);
	border-bottom-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 200);
	border-right-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 200);
	border-radius: token(radius-sm)px;
	color: token(text-emphasis);
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
}
.server-row:hover {
	decorator: linear-gradient(to bottom, #30363c, #171a1e 48%, #20252a);
	border-top-color: token(accent-steel-bright);
	border-left-color: token(accent-steel-bright);
}
.server-row:active {
	transform: translateY(1px);
}
.server-row.gray {
	color: token(semantic-neutral);
}
.server-row.orange {
	color: token(semantic-warning);
}

.server-gauge-slot {
	display: block;
	width: 200px;
	height: 5px;
	margin: 4px 0 0 9px;
	background-color: token(surface-0);
	decorator: repeating-linear-gradient(to right, #030303 0, #030303 17px, #222222 17px, #222222 20px);
}
.server-gauge-fill {
	display: block;
	height: 100%;
	background-color: #00bd8b;
}

#pvp_notice {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 420px;
	width: 480px;
	color: token(semantic-warning);
	font-size: 11px;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
}

#desc_panel {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 470px;
	width: 480px;
	color: token(text-body);
	white-space: normal;
	font-family: "token(font-body)";
}
